The attached image, Figure 2A and 2B from the PDF, visually characterizes Nano-11 nanoparticles. Figure 2A presents a transmission electron micrograph, revealing Nano-11 as spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like surface, primarily existing as single units or occasional pairs, with a scale bar indicating 50 nm. Figure 2B displays the hydrodynamic diameter distribution determined by dynamic light scattering, showing a uniform size range for Nano-11, with the Z-average diameter typically between 75 and 80 nm. This consistent particle size is highlighted in the text as critical for efficient uptake by dendritic cells, a key mechanism for its adjuvant effect.